===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*pьrvъ|gloss=first}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*pírˀwas}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*pr̥h₂wós}}, ultimately from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*per-||before, formerly; through, throughout}}.

Baltic cognates include {{cog|lt|pìrmas|t=first; primary}}, {{cog|lv|pìrmaĩs}}, {{cog|prg|pirmas|t=first}}.

Indo-European cognates include {{cog|sa|पूर्व|tr=pū́rva||foremost, first, previous}} and {{cog|en|fore}}.

